      "text": "The given equation is $7^{x+7} = 8^x$. Write this equation in logarithmic form to solve for $x$.\n\\begin{align*}\n7^{x+7} &= 8^x \\\\\n\\log_7 7^{x+7} &= \\log_7 8^x \\\\\n(x + 7) \\log_7 7 &= x \\log_7 8 \\\\\nx \\log_7 7 + 7 \\log_7 7 &= x \\log_7 8 \\\\\nx \\log_7 7 &= x \\log_7 8 - 7 \\log_7 7 \\\\\n\\log_7 7 &= \\log_7 8 - \\log_7 (x + 7) \\\\\n1 &= \\log_8 8 - \\log_7 (x + 7) \\\\\n1 &= \\log_8 8 - \\log_7 (x + 7) \\\\\n\\end{align*}\nTo solve for $x$, take the base $8$ logarithm of both sides of the equation:\n\\begin{align*}\n1 &= \\log_8 8 - \\log_7 (x + 7) \\\\\n\\log_8 8 &= \\log_8 8 - \\log_7 (x + 7) \\\\\n\\log_8 8 &= 0 + \\log_7 (x + 7)\n\\end{align*}\nSince $\\log_8 8$ is equivalent to $1$, we have:\n\\begin{align*}\n1 &= 1 + \\log_7 (x + 7) \\\\\n0 &= \\log_7 (x + 7)\n\\end{align*}\nSince $\\log_7 (x + 7) = 0$ is true when $x + 7 = 1$, we conclude that the solution to the equation is $x = \\boxed{-6}$.",
