      "text": "\\begin{align*}\n7^{x+7} &= 8^x \\\\\n7 \\cdot 7^x &= 8^x \\\\\n\\log_7 7 \\cdot \\log_7 7^x &= \\log_7 8^x\\\\\nx \\cdot \\log_7 7 &= x \\cdot \\log_7 8 \\\\\nx^{-\\log_7 7} &= x^{-\\log_7 8}\\\\\n7^{-\\log_7 7} &= 8^{-\\log_7 8}\\\\\nb &= \\boxed{8}\n\\end{align*}Alternatively:\n\\begin{align*}\n7^{x+7} &= 8^x \\\\\n7 \\cdot 7^x &= 8^x \\\\\n7 \\cdot 7^x &= 7^7 \\cdot 8^x \\\\\n\\frac{7^x}{7^7} &= \\frac{8^x}{7^7} \\\\\n7^x &= \\frac{7^x}{7^7} \\cdot 8^x \\\\\n\\frac{7^x}{7^x} &= \\frac{\\left( \\frac{8}{7} \\right)^x}{7^7} \\\\\n1 &= \\left( \\frac{8}{7} \\right)^x \\cdot 7^x \\\\\n\\left( \\frac{7}{8} \\cdot 7 \\right)^x = 1 \\\\\n\\left( \\frac{7}{8} \\cdot 7 \\right)^{-7} = 1,\n\\end{align*}so \\[\nx = \\boxed{\\frac{7}{8}}\n\\] as desired. The answer is \\frac{7}{8}",
